  <h1>Exchange Program</h1>
  <p>
    During the fall of 2024 I attended the University of Michigan's School of
    Information. I immersed myself in a diverse curriculum that bridged
    technical, ethical, and communicative aspects of information science. I
    developed practical skills in building data-driven web applications, using
    Django and Python. In "Automotive UX," I explored user experience design
    within the automotive industry, gaining insights into in-car interface
    development. "Introduction to Information Ethics" provided a framework for
    evaluating the ethical implications of information technologies, while
    "Intro to Project Management" equipped me with tools for managing
    non-repetitive business activities. "Interactive Communication" delved into
    the dynamics of digital communication, and "Editing and Style" honed my
    ability to craft clear, persuasive content. This experience broadened my
    perspective on information science and strengthened my ability to approach
    problems from multiple disciplines.
  </p>
